 ## Overview
-The Hybrid Multi-Space Module extends grid-based NeRF methods (such as iNGP and TensoRF) to handle multiple sub-spaces (e.g., reflections and refractions) by decomposing the multi-space composition information into a small MLP branch, while the main branch models multiple radiance fields using explicit grids [S1]. Unlike pure feature-field approaches, this module integrates discrete learnable grids with small MLPs to output densities and colors for each sub-space, enabling efficient rendering of complex light paths in grid-based architectures [S1]. It builds on [HybridNeRF Model Architecture](4842-hybridnerf-model-architecture.md).
+The Hybrid Multi-Space Module extends grid-based NeRF methods (such as iNGP and TensoRF) to handle multiple sub-spaces (e.g., reflections and refractions) by decomposing the multi-space composition information into a small MLP branch, while the main branch models multiple radiance fields using explicit grids [S1]. Unlike pure feature-field approaches, this module integrates discrete learnable grids with small MLPs to output densities and colors for each sub-space, enabling efficient rendering of complex light paths in grid-based architectures [S1]. It builds on [HybridNeRF Model Architecture](4842-hybridnerf-model-architecture.md) [S1].
 
